  <prompt>Drop the vestigial SEPARATE Dataverse S2S app-registration (`spaarke-dataverse-s2s-*`) + its `Dataverse-S2S-ClientId`/`Dataverse-S2S-ClientSecret` Key Vault secrets + rotation ceremony from provisioning/deploy/docs. GROUNDED 2026-08-13: this app-reg has ZERO code consumers (grep `Dataverse-S2S|DATAVERSE_CLIENT_ID` across `src/` → none; consolidated to `API_CLIENT_SECRET` on 2026-01-07 per docs/architecture/auth-azure-resources.md:407) — it survives only in provisioning scripts + docs + KV. This delivers r1's literal "2 app-regs → 1" ask with NO BFF code change. **NOT in scope here**: migrating the BFF's OWN shared-lib Dataverse path (`DataverseServiceClientImpl`/`DataverseWebApiService`) from `ClientSecret` (the BFF app-reg's `API_CLIENT_SECRET`) to managed identity — that is #3(b), an identity-attribution change entangled with the two access stacks, deferred to the NG1 / task-011 assess-then-decide track (see notes/deployment-refactors-assessment-2026-08-12.md §Addendum 2026-08-13).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer with auth v2 / ADR-028 + Entra provisioning expertise. Remove dead auth infrastructure only; do NOT change any BFF credential code path in this task. Follow ADR-028; preserve OBO + SpeAdmin per-tenant secrets verbatim.</role>
  <goal>The separate `spaarke-dataverse-s2s-*` app-reg is no longer created/tested by provisioning, its `Dataverse-S2S-*` KV secrets + rotation are removed from scripts + docs, and the stale "MI rejected for Dataverse" doc claim is corrected — with a re-grounding safety check proving zero code consumers first, and OBO + the BFF's own (still-secret) Dataverse path left untouched.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Refactor ask #3 (notes/deployment-complexity-refactors-ask-2026-08-12.md) accepted 2026-08-13, SPLIT by owner decision: #3(a) = this task (clean vestigial-app-reg drop); #3(b) = the shared-lib ClientSecret→MI migration, routed to the NG1/task-011 track (the assessment doc §Addendum 2026-08-13 carries the full (b) grounding). Grounded facts for (a): the separate S2S app-reg (`spaarke-dataverse-s2s-prod` etc.) has ZERO code consumers — `grep Dataverse-S2S|DATAVERSE_CLIENT_ID` across src/ returns nothing; it was consolidated to `API_CLIENT_SECRET` on 2026-01-07 (auth-azure-resources.md:407). It survives only in: scripts/Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 (:8,:42-43,:71,:81,:435-509,:629,:639-640 — creates the app-reg + writes Dataverse-S2S-* KV secrets), scripts/Test-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 (:8,:268-277,:330-331), scripts/README.md (:323-324), docs/guides/SECRET-ROTATION-PROCEDURES.md (:58,:239-251), docs/architecture/auth-azure-resources.md (:825-852), docs/architecture/AZURE-RESOURCE-NAMING-CONVENTION.md (:153,:186,:349), docs/guides/INCIDENT-RESPONSE.md (:564), PRODUCTION-/SPAARKE-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE, and the stale docs/guides/DATAVERSE-AUTHENTICATION-GUIDE.md:1007 ("Managed Identity: Rejected — doesn't work for Dataverse S2S"), which contradicts ADR-028:24 + the live auth-deployment-setup.md §9c smoke test. ADR-028 needs NO amendment (ADR-028:24 already mandates MI for the Dataverse service identity).</background>
