  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (provisioning/docs/KV ONLY): drop the separate `spaarke-dataverse-s2s-*` app-reg creation/testing + `Dataverse-S2S-ClientId`/`Dataverse-S2S-ClientSecret` KV writes + rotation from the enumerated scripts/docs. Do NOT edit any BFF source file. Do NOT touch the BFF's own Dataverse credential path (that is #3(b) / task 011).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">DO NOT remove or alter `BFF-API-ClientSecret` / `API_CLIENT_SECRET` (used by OBO AND, until #3(b) lands, the shared-lib Dataverse path) or `Dataverse-ClientSecret`. Only the `Dataverse-S2S-*` secrets of the vestigial separate app-reg are dropped. Preserve SpeAdmin per-tenant container-type app-reg secrets (ADR-028:24 exception 1) verbatim.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (safety gate, prescriptive): re-run the zero-consumer grep FIRST. If ANY code (src/) or live runtime config references the separate S2S app-reg / `Dataverse-S2S-*` / `DATAVERSE_CLIENT_ID`, STOP (escalation) — it is not vestigial and this task's premise is wrong.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§10">Scope: no BFF publish-size impact (no Sprk.Bff.Api source/appsettings change) — state this explicitly. Run /conflict-check before the PR (shared provisioning scripts). Coordinate with customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1 (it provisions app-regs; its design drops the S2S app-reg from §9.1 after this lands).</constraint>
    <constraint source="auth-gate">GATED on the BFF Auth Surface Map (task 019 → notes/bff-auth-surface-map.md). Before deleting any secret/app-reg, confirm against the map's secret/identity→consumer dependency graph that the target (`Dataverse-S2S-*` / the separate S2S app-reg) has NO consumers — the map is the authoritative "safe-to-remove" verdict, not just this task's grep.</constraint>
    <constraint source="auth-map-2026-08-13">Map riders (extend the safety gate + doc scope): (1) BEFORE deleting the S2S app-registration itself, re-grep `.github/workflows/` for a `DATAVERSE_CLIENT_ID` GitHub secret used by CI `pac` pipelines (SPAARKE-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md:1634-1638) — if a live workflow consumes it, STOP/escalate. **Verified 2026-08-13: CLEARED — no workflow references `DATAVERSE_CLIENT_ID`/`DATAVERSE_CLIENT_SECRET`, no such repo secret exists, and deploy workflows use OIDC federated login (`azure/login@v2`); the deployment-guide reference is stale. Re-verify at execution (things change), but there is currently no CI consumer.** (2) While editing auth-azure-resources.md, ALSO fix its stale identity claims: :274-284 says "system-assigned" but the MI is a **UAMI** (`mi-bff-api-dev` clientId 5967251e…/`mi-bff-api-demo` b0ce4ca4…; `56ae2188…` is a RETIRED principal), and :705-708 contradicts :349 on which secret is in KV `BFF-API-ClientSecret` (**RESOLVED 2026-08-13 via config/environments.json:22,26 — `BFF-API-ClientSecret` holds the BFF app-reg `1e40baad-…` secret; the `170c98e1-…` in :705-708 is the SDAP-PCF-CLIENT SPA/`msalClient`, NOT the BFF secret — fix :705-708 to say `1e40baad`. Dev vault = `spaarke-spekvcert`; demo/prod = `sprk-platform-prod-kv`**). Do NOT touch `BFF-API-ClientSecret`/`Dataverse-ClientSecret` (map: one KV secret, 5 config keys, 9 consumers — never-remove; the Dataverse-app-only consumers only disappear after the #3b migration on the task-011 track).</constraint>
    <constraint source="net10-2026-08-14">Environment reality (handback `notes/r3-handoff.md`): **only `spaarke-dev` is live** — demo/prod were decommissioned for budget. Any "in BOTH spaarkedev1 + spaarke-demo" verification is **dev-only for now**; demo/prod cleanup is DEFERRED until those envs are re-provisioned on net10 (a separate follow-on, not this task).</constraint>
  </constraints>

