  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the rigor-level declaration (STANDARD + auth-adjacent reason). Load ADR-028 + the assessment §Addendum 2026-08-13; run /conflict-check on the scripts.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Safety gate — re-ground zero consumers">grep `Dataverse-S2S|DATAVERSE_CLIENT_ID|spaarke-dataverse-s2s` across src/ AND live runtime config. Expect ZERO in src/. If any live consumer exists, STOP and escalate — do not remove a still-used app-reg.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Provisioning">Remove the S2S app-reg creation + `Dataverse-S2S-*` KV writes from Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1; remove the S2S test block from Test-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Rotation + docs">Drop the S2S rotation schedule from SECRET-ROTATION-PROCEDURES.md; remove S2S app-reg references from scripts/README.md, auth-azure-resources.md, AZURE-RESOURCE-NAMING-CONVENTION.md, INCIDENT-RESPONSE.md, PRODUCTION-/SPAARKE-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Fix stale doc">Correct DATAVERSE-AUTHENTICATION-GUIDE.md:1007 — MI is mandated for the Dataverse service identity per ADR-028:24; note the shared-lib ClientSecret→MI migration (#3(b)) is tracked on the NG1/task-011 track (not this task).</step>
    <step order="5" name="Operator KV note">Record an operator KV-deletion checklist in task notes naming ONLY `Dataverse-S2S-ClientId` + `Dataverse-S2S-ClientSecret` (explicitly NOT `BFF-API-ClientSecret`/`Dataverse-ClientSecret`, which the OBO + shared-lib Dataverse paths still use).</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set task 060 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 if the safety-gate grep finds ANY live code or runtime-config consumer of the separate Dataverse S2S app-reg / `Dataverse-S2S-*` / `DATAVERSE_CLIENT_ID` — the "vestigial, zero-consumer" premise would be false and dropping it could break a live app-only Dataverse path.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="config">scripts/Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 + Test-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 (S2S sections removed)</output>
