  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Safety gate: grep of src/ for `Dataverse-S2S|DATAVERSE_CLIENT_ID|spaarke-dataverse-s2s` returns zero (recorded in notes) BEFORE any removal.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 + Test-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 no longer create/test the separate Dataverse S2S app-reg or write `Dataverse-S2S-*` KV secrets; SECRET-ROTATION-PROCEDURES.md no longer schedules their rotation.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Repo-wide grep for `Dataverse-S2S` / `spaarke-dataverse-s2s` in scripts/ + docs/guides/ + docs/architecture/ returns no live-procedure references (historical project notes exempt).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (untouched): `BFF-API-ClientSecret`/`API_CLIENT_SECRET`/`Dataverse-ClientSecret` are unchanged; no Sprk.Bff.Api source or appsettings edited; the BFF still boots and serves Dataverse via its existing (still-secret) path; SpeAdmin per-tenant secrets untouched.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">DATAVERSE-AUTHENTICATION-GUIDE.md:1007 no longer claims MI is rejected for Dataverse; it points to ADR-028:24 + the NG1/task-011 migration track.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Operator KV-deletion checklist names ONLY `Dataverse-S2S-*` (not the OBO/shared-lib secrets); no BFF publish-size impact stated.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Refactor ask #3(a) — clean vestigial-app-reg drop; delivers r1's "2 app-regs → 1". #3(b) (shared-lib ClientSecret→MI migration; identity-attribution change; the two-access-stack files) is DEFERRED to the NG1 / task-011 assess-then-decide track — full grounding in notes/deployment-refactors-assessment-2026-08-12.md §Addendum 2026-08-13; flagged by task 040 rule (c) until 011's design lands it. Correction of record: my 2026-08-12 assessment wrongly said the credential half was fully landed — only the Services/Ai raw-HTTP camp was (AUTHV2-042); the shared-lib camp is still secret-based.</notes>

